## Self-updating pipelines

Nornir volumes rebuild themselves. Each stage records what it was built from (input checksums, transform and
filter attributes) and, when its input changes, regenerates its output on the next pipeline run. Derived data
needs no management by hand.

- **Change the input, then re-run the pipelines.** After replacing a filter (e.g. a section's Raw filter), a
  mosaic or other input, run the normal stages; dependent outputs (Blob, Mask, Leveled, assemblies, tilesets,
  VikingXML) rebuild because their recorded inputs no longer match.
- **Leave stale outputs in place.** Do not delete, rename or hand-patch derived filters, tilesets or mosaics to
  "clean up" after an input change; the stage that owns them replaces them.
- **Keep volumes in their normal form.** No parallel copies of filters, extra VikingXML files or backups inside
  a volume; anything outside a volume's usual layout becomes manual cleanup later. Backups and experiments go
  outside the volume (e.g. `Y:\_nornir_work\<topic>\`).
- **A stage that misses an input change is a bug.** Report it (or fix it in the stage's validity check); do not
  work around it with manual deletions, which hides the bug and breaks the self-updating design.
